            {
              ":answer/id": "3275b7d6-8751-5d17-9647-5df225d409f1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k{B}^{2}(452-B)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "9a699607-71ef-505b-93fc-5a9a3fde04fb"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate of change is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-B),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity and $k>0$.\n\nHere $a=452$ cultures, so\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k(452-B).\n$$"
