      ":question/id": "79dfba0b-24db-5664-b4c9-d12274cb27d0",
      ":question/problem": "A laboratory incubator initially contains $21$ cultures, and its maximum capacity is $452$ cultures. Let $B(t)$ be the number of cultures, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in days. Its population obeys an inhibited growth model. The rate of increase equals $5$ times the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Which differential equation models this population?",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
